1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,800
Your data has connections. Your AI needs
context. I built Arkiv Graph to

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:05,960
bring them together.

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:13,023
Built on Arkiv, it connects signed records
into graphs. A complete manifest

4
00:00:13,053 --> 00:00:16,371
lets another reader verify every member
and relationship.

5
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:25,944
Follow a task to its context and original
sources. Verify the bytes, then

6
00:00:25,974 --> 00:00:30,424
deliver bounded evidence to AI. Only
selected, verified context reaches

7
00:00:30,454 --> 00:00:31,400
the model.

8
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:35,933
Choose a task. Its graph connects the
sources and current reviews.

9
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:42,397
Qarinah selects two current events. One
source excerpt becomes

10
00:00:42,427 --> 00:00:43,427
untrusted evidence.

11
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:49,000
Open the exact evidence message. Its byte
identity is checked in your browser.

12
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:54,668
The model runs. Tests check its guard. A
receipt binds the reported inputs

13
00:00:54,698 --> 00:00:55,448
and result.

14
00:00:56,150 --> 00:01:00,775
AI Passport puts it to work. A real model
builds a guard that passes

15
00:01:00,805 --> 00:01:01,853
six boundary tests.

16
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:05,601
AI Passport also has source-linked
learning tools.

17
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:10,784
Its safety game cites the original NPCI
guidance.

18
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:15,976
Withdraw a required review, and this
evidence gate stops inference.

19
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:22,532
Two separate readers verify the same
graph, source bytes, and current review.

20
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:28,710
Each makes a fresh read. Both admit the
task. Six guard tests pass, without

21
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:29,449
a model.

22
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:35,679
The reviewer withdraws its review in a new
Arkiv transaction.

23
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:41,828
Once visible, B reads again. Its next task
is refused.

24
00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:46,572
A makes its own fresh read. The task is
refused too.

25
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:52,852
Both clients and wallets belong to this
project. Every new task checks again.

26
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:59,855
Install the public SDK. Build a browser,
Node, or MCP reader that verifies

27
00:01:59,885 --> 00:02:01,263
Arkiv records locally.

28
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:06,211
Arkiv Graph. Connected evidence for useful
AI. Try it now.
